  "market_facts": "About 5% of suppliers with 5+ years on the platform, and 30% of those with 0-2 years, ship bad lots: a bad supplier's units are defective 30% of the time (a good one's 1%), it is on time 85% of the time (good 97%), and 45% of its orders have a problem (good 5%). About 35% of genuine orders get a review. Genuine orders average 18 a year for established suppliers and 6 a year for newer ones (a supplier under a year old counts as half a year). Ratings run high: a review of an order without a problem gives 5/4/3/2/1 stars with probability 86%/12%/1.5%/0.5%/0%, and of an order with a problem 30%/25%/20%/15%/10%. 25% of bad suppliers buy fake orders, on average 6, each with a five-star review; fake orders count in the order total but are never protected. The on-time record counts only protected orders (about 60% of orders). Gold is a paid membership held by 60% of suppliers of either kind; Verified checks the company, not the product (50% of good and 35% of bad suppliers hold it). Reply speed says nothing about quality. A sample inspects a batch of units and reports how many were defective; batches can be repeated and their counts accumulate. After each period the history shows, for every lot delivered, whether it arrived on time and, if it did, how many of its units were defective; a late lot shows no defect count.",
